```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant ADM  as Administrator
    participant AGT  as agent_openai.py
    participant LLM  as OpenAI Responses API
    participant MCP  as mcp-grafana MCP Server
    participant GRAF as Grafana Cloud
    participant ALRT as Grafana Alerting
    participant LOKI as Loki Logs
    participant TEMP as Tempo Traces
    participant K8S  as Kubernetes / Online Boutique

    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
        Note over K8S,GRAF: Application is deployed with Skaffold and emits telemetry
        ADM->>K8S: skaffold dev / skaffold run
        K8S->>GRAF: Metrics, logs and traces are collected
        GRAF->>ALRT: Alert rules are evaluated
        GRAF->>LOKI: Logs are available for querying
        GRAF->>TEMP: Traces are available for querying
    end

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
        Note over ADM,ALRT: Test 1 — auto-triage with no active alerts

        ADM->>AGT: python agent_openai.py --triage
        AGT->>MCP: Start MCP server via uvx mcp-grafana
        MCP->>GRAF: Authenticate with Grafana service account token
        AGT->>MCP: initialize MCP session
        AGT->>MCP: list_tools
        MCP-->>AGT: Grafana MCP tools returned
        AGT->>AGT: Filter tools: alert, loki, log, tempo, trace
        AGT->>MCP: list_loki_label_names
        MCP->>LOKI: Fetch available Loki labels
        LOKI-->>MCP: Label names returned
        MCP-->>AGT: Known Loki labels

        AGT->>LLM: System prompt + triage query + MCP tool schemas
        LLM-->>AGT: function_call: alerting_manage_rules
        AGT->>MCP: alerting_manage_rules(states=firing,pending)
        MCP->>ALRT: Query firing and pending alerts
        ALRT-->>MCP: No firing or pending alerts
        MCP-->>AGT: Empty alert result
        AGT->>LLM: function_call_output with alert result

        LLM-->>AGT: Final answer: no active alerts to investigate
        AGT-->>ADM: Print triage result in terminal
    end

    rect rgb(245, 255, 245)
        Note over ADM,LOKI: Test 2 — targeted question about kube-apiserver errors

        ADM->>AGT: python agent_openai.py -q "Analyze kube-apiserver logs for errors"
        AGT->>LLM: User question + system prompt + MCP tool schemas

        LLM-->>AGT: function_call: list_loki_label_names
        AGT->>MCP: list_loki_label_names(datasourceUid=grafanacloud-logs)
        MCP->>LOKI: Fetch Loki label names
        LOKI-->>MCP: Labels such as job, container, pod, namespace
        MCP-->>AGT: Label names
        AGT->>LLM: function_call_output with labels

        LLM-->>AGT: function_call: list_loki_label_values
        AGT->>MCP: list_loki_label_values(labelName=job/container/pod)
        MCP->>LOKI: Search label values related to kube-apiserver
        LOKI-->>MCP: Matching Kubernetes label values
        MCP-->>AGT: Label values
        AGT->>LLM: function_call_output with label values

        LLM-->>AGT: function_call: query_loki_logs
        AGT->>MCP: query_loki_logs(LogQL for kube-apiserver error-like logs)
        MCP->>LOKI: Query logs containing error, failed, denied, timeout, panic
        LOKI-->>MCP: kube-apiserver error log lines
        MCP-->>AGT: Error logs with timestamps and labels
        AGT->>LLM: function_call_output with log results

        LLM-->>AGT: Final summary of recurring error patterns
        AGT-->>ADM: Print log analysis in terminal
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 235)
        Note over ADM,GRAF: Manual verification in Grafana UI
        ADM->>GRAF: Open Grafana Explore
        GRAF->>LOKI: Display kube-apiserver logs
        LOKI-->>GRAF: Error logs visible in dashboard
        ADM->>ADM: Compare Grafana logs with agent summary
    end
```
